{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 25, :comments ["<b>And Yishmael his son was thirteen years old</b> etc. This verse comes to teach us that on the same day that Avraham was circumcised, Yishmael was circumcised, and this is derived from 'בעצם היום הזה' (on the very selfsame day). And from the verse 'בעצם היום הזה' we also know that Yishmael was thirteen years old when he was circumcised, for it is written 'ואברם בן שמונים שנה ושש שנים' when Hagar bore Yishmael to him, and it is written 'ואברהם בן תשעים ותשע שנה בהמולו,' and they were circumcised on one day, as we said. If so, we know automatically that he was thirteen years old when circumcised, and the verse 'and Yishmael his son was thirteen years old when he was circumcised' — why do I need it? Rather, this verse comes to teach you: just as Avram did not delay, so Yishmael did not delay — that is what it comes for." "<b>Et the flesh of his foreskin.</b> Rashi explained: Yishmael, who was a child, required cutting the foreskin and peeling back the circumcision; therefore the word 'את' is stated regarding him. And even though we say in Yevamot that 'pri'ah' (peeling back) had not yet been given, nevertheless Avraham our father observed it, and likewise 'eruvei tavshilin.'"], :book :genesis, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 17, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:04:34.124863713Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}